# API, Auth, Security

## Auth

- Email register/login: bcrypt password hashes + JWT (`JWT_SECRET`, HS256, ~30 days).
- Google login currently bridges Emergent (`auth.emergentagent.com` + session-data endpoint). New Google work should plan a first-party OAuth path and keep `.env.example` honest.
- Apple login is a UI placeholder — do not claim it works.
- Protect user routes with `get_current_user` / existing Depends patterns.

## API

- Prefix `/api`.
- Validate inputs with Pydantic.
- Return consistent error details; do not leak stack traces to clients.

## Secrets

- Never commit `.env`, tokens, credentials JSON, vault keys.
- Update `backend/.env.example` and `frontend/.env.example` when adding config.
- Token vault: `TOKEN_VAULT_BACKEND` / `TOKEN_VAULT_KEY` — do not log decrypted secrets.
- Google Calendar OAuth needs `GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID`, `GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET`, `GOOGLE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI`.

## Security checklist on auth/API changes

- AuthN + AuthZ on sensitive routes
- Input validation
- No secret in responses/logs
- Session/token handling unchanged or improved
- Dependency risk considered
